From: "Phase1 Draft (Claude, for Terhi review)" <draft@local>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:37:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] refactor(sim): _sim_cox rates from the likelihood's
 atoms; conditional draws unchanged. N ~ Poisson(Ig * Ih) with Ig =
 seasonal_time_integral total and Ih = sum of the eq. 24 mass vector -- i.e.
 the Poisson mean is the likelihood's Itot_time times its Itot_xy BY
 CONSTRUCTION (spatial_refinement_integral is literally that sum since the
 previous commit): (I1) and the background count normalizer of (I11) are
 structural. SCOPE, stated precisely per review: this makes the count
 NORMALIZER shared; full conservation remains structural only for rectangular
 or exact-refinement domains -- non-rectangular GeoDataFrame boundary cells
 are sampled over the full cell then clipped, out-of-domain offspring can
 parent before clipping, and finite spatial_window is event-side only (all
 documented in the I11 test and the _sim_cox docstring); SBC stays restricted
 to rectangular domains with spatial_window=None. One mass vector drives BOTH
 the count rate and the conditional cell draw (self-normalized); breakpoint
 masses still drive the conditional time draw (self-normalized, normalization
 == Ig to float precision, tested). New shared _sample_cells primitive
 (length-guarded) used here and, next commit, by the pure-Hawkes background.
 Covariate branch's inline log_h/area deleted (the atom supplies masses for
 both branches). Verified: 37/37; inference value+gradient pins bit-identical.

